  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Right in the middle of the culinary duel, Gulya pulls Lyova aside to tell him she is leaving for Bishkek forever. Distracted and heartbroken, Lyova ruins his dish, and a brawl breaks out on the kitchen floor, ending the contest.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Гуля, я не могу говорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Подожди, это сейчас очень важно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Я пыталась тебе сегодня сказать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Я уезжаю в Бишкек навсегда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Прощай, Лёва, не ищи меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Подожди, как это ты уезжаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Шеф, простите меня за блюдо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лёва, ты куда сейчас побежал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Смотри вперёд, разуй свои глаза!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Продолжать поединок уже нет смысла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Гуля, скажи, ты сейчас пошутила?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Если пошутила, это не смешно.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Гуля, я не могу говорить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Gulya, I cannot talk right now.' Notice how Russian expresses 'Gulya' and 'to speak' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Gulya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Подожди, это сейчас очень важно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, this is very important right now.' The meaning hinges on 'wait' working together with 'important' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Я пыталась тебе сегодня сказать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I tried to tell you today.' Gulya addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'to say'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Я уезжаю в Бишкек навсегда.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am leaving for Bishkek forever.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'I' and finishing on 'forever'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "gulya",
      "t": "Прощай, Лёва, не ищи меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Farewell, Lyova, do not look for me.' Gulya brings out the contrast between 'farewell' and 'Lyova' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Подожди, как это ты уезжаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Wait, what do you mean you are leaving?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'wait' and finishing on 'are leaving'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Шеф, простите меня за блюдо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, forgive me for the dish.' Lyova brings out the contrast between 'Chef Barinov' and 'forgive' in a few short words. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Лёва, ты куда сейчас побежал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Lyova, where are you running off to now?' Notice how Russian expresses 'Lyova' and 'ran' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Смотри вперёд, разуй свои глаза!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Look ahead, open your eyes wide!' The grammar packs 'watch' and 'eyes' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Продолжать поединок уже нет смысла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There is no point in continuing the duel now.' The meaning hinges on 'to continue' working together with 'sense' in spoken Russian. Lyova answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Гуля, скажи, ты сейчас пошутила?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Gulya, tell me, were you joking just now?' The grammar packs 'Gulya' and 'was joking' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Если пошутила, это не смешно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'If you were joking, it is not funny.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'if' and finishing on 'ridiculous'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
